{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789028578,"nonce":"tMEkhkvWxzUQsij803Yanh/REKE=","message":"Measured, and this is bigger than 'the JIT still reads opcodes'. The LLVM backend does not translate AIR at all: it ROUND-TRIPS through HL opcodes.\n\n  Instr variants in AIR v2                          56\n  variants air_instr_opcode rebuilds into opcodes    55\n  emitted as LLVM IR directly                    5 vector ops, plus Pos\n\nSo translate_air_v2 walks AIR, reconstructs an HL opcode per instruction, and\nhands it to translate_opcode -- the same emitter the raw path uses. Two places\nin air_emit show the cost directly: FieldGet temporarily overwrites\nlowering.regs[ri] to smuggle AIR's resolved obj_ty past an opcode that cannot\ncarry it, and SetEnumField fabricates an EnumAlloc because the legacy primitive\ndiscovers the construct by SCANNING PRECEDING OPCODES. Both exist only because\nthe typed SSA form was thrown away a step earlier.\n\nThere are four lowering paths in the tree, not two:\n\n  LLVM (hybrid promote, AOT)   AIR -\u003e rebuilt opcodes -\u003e LLVM   opcode.rs\n  Cranelift codegen.rs         AIR -\u003e CLIF directly             60 instrs\n  Cranelift lower.rs           opcodes -\u003e CLIF                  114 opcodes\n  interpreter                  SSA walker, plus an opcode walker\n\nThat is why the same decision gets made differently in different places.\nConcrete instance found today: cranelift/lower.rs coerce widens with an\nunconditional sextend under the comment 'HashLink integers are signed', while\nthe LLVM side tests src_kind and zero-extends HUI8/HUI16 -- so hl.UI8\narithmetic reads 144 in three engines and -112 in the fourth (9c5e47e). A\ncounter at the top of translate_opcode: hybrid 23 calls, AOT 4385, --mode jit\n0.\n\nRaising this off backlog. It is not tidiness -- it is the structural reason\ncorrectness fixes have to be written more than once and drift apart.","files":null}]}